{"name":"Purple’s Baby Sister","hex":"#eec3ee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.\n\nA very young human, even if not yet born.","A very young human, even if not yet born."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"sister","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A daughter of the same parents as another person; a female sibling.","A female member of a religious order; especially one devoted to more active service;  a nun."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strengthen (a supporting beam) by fastening a second beam alongside it.","To be sister to; to resemble closely."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sister"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infant","blocks":[{"text":"An infant is a very young human being. Baby is an alternative term for infant. The terms may also be used to refer to juvenile beings of other organisms. A newborn is, in mainstream use, an infant who is only hours, days, or weeks old; while in medical contexts, a newborn or neonate is an infant in the first 28 days after birth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg/330px-The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infant"},{"title":"Sister","blocks":[{"text":"A sister is a woman or a girl who shares parents or a parent with another individual; a female sibling. The male counterpart is a brother. Although the term typically refers to a familial relationship, it is sometimes used endearingly to refer to non-familial relationships. A full sister is a first-degree relative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Little_Julia_tending_the_baby_at_home.jpg/330px-Little_Julia_tending_the_baby_at_home.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sister"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg/330px-Views_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AViews_of_a_Foetus_in_the_Womb_detail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Baby_Face.JPG/500px-Baby_Face.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Baby_Face.JPG/1280px-Baby_Face.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Baby_Face.JPG/500px-Baby_Face.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eight-month-old infant; as a common feature, eyes are usually large in relation to the face.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaby_Face.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Baby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg/500px-Baby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Baby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg/500px-Baby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thin brown hair of a one-year-old infant girl","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaby_hairy_head_DSCN2483.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/HumanNewborn.JPG/500px-HumanNewborn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/HumanNewborn.JPG/1280px-HumanNewborn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/HumanNewborn.JPG/500px-HumanNewborn.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A newborn infant, seconds after delivery. Amniotic fluid 